# The parity suite compares captured reference output BYTE FOR BYTE, and 486 of the
# goldens contain bare CR characters — the reference's own `\r`-separated progress
# tokens (`10%20%…`), which are mid-line, not line terminators. Git for Windows
# defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which would rewrite those files on checkout and
# make every affected case fail on a platform where nothing is actually wrong.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line translation for these paths, on every platform.
# Do not relax it: a golden is evidence, and evidence must survive a checkout.
tests/parity/golden/** -text

# Same reasoning: these are the reference's own cached canvas readings (see
# docs/MAINTAINING.md §8.3). They are data, not source.
docs/research/fixtures/*_measured.json -text

# The recorded parity outcome CI asserts against, compared line by line.
tests/parity/BASELINE.txt -text
